      "writtenOn": "2020-07-07T18:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we enabling this in baseboard?\n\nThis throws off the RO rwsig assumption.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/master:src/platform/ec/board/nucleo-dartmonkey/board.h;l\u003d46-50?ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch:src%2Fplatform%2Fec\n\nWe already enable this in RW where we need it for FP stuff.",
      "revId": "ab022e1797d199832c0449a85215298b16067127",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec5cd9de_c36f9e0c",
        "filename": "baseboard/nucleo-f412zg/base-board.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-08T20:12:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was for testing on-device tests that use the new shared_mem (malloc), see http://crrev/c/2242354. Since we actually use it in RW, tests should also use this new shared_mem (malloc). Maybe we should not run the utils test on nucleo-f412zg and nucleo-h743zi, but only run utils test on fingerprint boards.\n\nAlternatively, if we still run utils test on these nucleo boards, we disable CONFIG_MALLOC like you said, and the tests will use the old common/share_mem.c. We may want to add a comment in that case, it took me one afternoon to figure out there are two implementations of shared_mem!",
      "parentUuid": "233c43cb_9ce8704c",
      "revId": "ab022e1797d199832c0449a85215298b16067127",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb524197_001abff0",
        "filename": "baseboard/nucleo-f412zg/base-board.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-10T16:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think both implementations should be tested, but that utils test that you mention in http://crrev/c/2242354 looks pretty specific to the classic shared_mem single-shot allocator. The shmalloc seems to be tested in https://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/test/shmalloc.c and is enabled specifically in https://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/test/test_config.h#L233 .\n\nYou can enable test specific configs in the following file, but again, I don\u0027t think you want to enable CONFIG_MALLOC for that util test:\nhttps://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/test/test_config.h",
      "parentUuid": "ec5cd9de_c36f9e0c",
      "revId": "ab022e1797d199832c0449a85215298b16067127",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
